Fluorescent Protein, have revolutionized the observation&#10;and measurement of cellular states. However, the inverse&#10;challenge of using light to precisely control cellular&#10;behavior has only recently begun to be addressed; sem...&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 2&#10;domain: same_field&#10;radius: R1&#10;title: Editorial: Insights in nanobiotechnology 2024/2025:&#10;novel developments, current challenges, and future&#10;perspectives&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['Mechanism–microenvironment–time as an&#10;organizing principle for controlling nano-bio behavior',&#10;'Quantitative treatment of biological timing, heterogeneity,&#10;and synchrony rather than treating them as nuisance&#10;variables', 'Computational design frameworks for organ-on-chip&#10;systems that model gradients, forces, and context-dependent&#10;cell fate', 'Context-dependent steering of biological systems&#10;toward reproducible, mechanistically explained states']&#10;combination_plan: Use the candidate’s mechanism-&#10;microenvironment-time framework to structure the living-&#10;material programming problem as a multi-scale closed-loop&#10;control system, where molecular interfacing, metabolite&#10;sensing, genetic regulation, and matrix remodeling are coupled&#10;through explic...&#10;justification: Although the candidate is an editorial rather&#10;than a specific method paper, it articulates a transferable&#10;abstraction: robust control of complex bio-interfaces requires&#10;mechanistic modeling, microenvironmental context, and explicit&#10;temporal dynamics. This maps directly onto th...&#10;abstract: Nanobiotechnology is progressing rapidly, and the&#10;last few years have brought a noticeable shift in what the&#10;community expects as proof. Advances in nanomaterial design,&#10;characterization, and experimental models now make it possible&#10;to ask more demanding questions: not only wh...&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 3&#10;domain: computer_science&#10;radius: R2&#10;title: Towards Big Biology:: high-performance verification of&#10;large concurrent systems&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['formal verification of large concurrent&#10;systems', 'compositional model checking of interacting&#10;processes', 'temporal-logic specification of safety, liveness,&#10;and ordering constraints', 'runtime verification / closed-loop&#10;monitoring of concurrent state transitions', 'scalable&#10;abstraction-reduction methods for high-dimensional biological&#10;dynamics']&#10;combination_plan: Treat the living-material program as a&#10;concurrent system whose modules—protein-material conjugation,&#10;metabolite sensing, genetic regulation, and matrix&#10;remodeling—are verified as interacting processes with temporal&#10;constraints. Use compositional formal verification or&#10;runtime...&#10;justification: Even without the abstract, the title indicates&#10;high-performance verification of large concurrent systems,&#10;which provides a transferable abstraction for coordinating&#10;many interacting biological control loops. The problem’s core&#10;bottleneck is not just building biological parts b...&#10;abstract:&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 4&#10;domain: computer_science&#10;radius: R2&#10;title: Formal Verification for Natural and Engineered&#10;Biological Systems&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['formal specification of desired&#10;biological behavior using temporal logic or safety/liveness&#10;properties', 'model checking or reachability analysis for&#10;predicting system trajectories under coupled molecular,&#10;cellular, and matrix-level dynamics', 'verification of&#10;orthogonality, viability, and spatiotemporal constraints as&#10;formal invariants', 'compositional verification for&#10;integrating molecular interfacing, sensing, genetic&#10;regulation, and extracellular remodeling modules']&#10;combination_plan: Cast the living-material programming problem&#10;as a formally specified closed-loop control system, where&#10;viability, orthogonality, and spatiotemporal activation are&#10;encoded as temporal-logic constraints. Use mechanistic models&#10;of conjugation, metabolite sensing, gene regulation,...&#10;justification: The candidate paper’s core abstraction is&#10;formal verification of biological systems through&#10;computational models and rigorous property checking. This&#10;directly maps to the problem’s need for a unified, predictive,&#10;closed-loop framework that can guarantee coordinated multi-&#10;scale...&#10;abstract: Computational modeling is now used effectively to&#10;complement experimental work in biology, allowing to identify&#10;gaps in our understanding of the biological systems studied,&#10;and to predict system behavior based on a mechanistic model.We&#10;provide an overview of several areas in b...&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 5&#10;domain: control_engineering&#10;radius: R2&#10;title: Systems and control theoretic approaches to engineer&#10;robust biological systems&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['closed-loop feedback control&#10;architecture for biological systems', 'robustness and&#10;stability analysis under biological uncertainty', 'predictive&#10;or model-based control for dynamic regulation', 'orthogonal&#10;control channels and modular system decomposition', 'sensing-&#10;actuation loops linking intracellular state to extracellular&#10;outputs']&#10;combination_plan: Use systems-and-control theory to formalize&#10;the living-material platform as a multi-input/multi-output&#10;closed-loop system, where molecular interfacing, metabolite&#10;sensing, genetic regulation, and matrix remodeling are modeled&#10;as coupled subsystems with feedback, feedforward, a...&#10;justification: The candidate paper’s focus on systems and&#10;control theoretic engineering of robust biological systems&#10;provides a direct transferable abstraction for the original&#10;problem’s central bottleneck: creating a unified, predictive,&#10;closed-loop programming framework across molecular, c...&#10;abstract:&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 6&#10;domain: control_engineering&#10;radius: R2&#10;title: A computational framework for optimal and Model&#10;Predictive Control of stochastic gene regulatory networks&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['stochastic model predictive control&#10;(MPC) for gene regulatory networks', 'optimal closed-loop&#10;feedback under molecular noise', 'constraint-aware control&#10;design for biological viability', 'receding-horizon predictive&#10;coordination of biomolecular states', 'cybergenetic control&#10;architecture for cellular functions']&#10;combination_plan: Adapt the candidate’s stochastic&#10;MPC/cybergenetic framework into a unified controller for the&#10;living-material system, using noisy measurements of&#10;metabolites, genetic states, and matrix remodeling to predict&#10;future system trajectories and optimize light inputs,&#10;transport cues,...&#10;justification: The candidate provides a direct structural&#10;analogy: a predictive, optimal, noise-aware closed-loop&#10;control framework for biological regulation. This maps onto&#10;the problem’s missing unified programming layer for&#10;coordinating heterogeneous biological processes while&#10;respecting v...&#10;abstract: Engineering biology requires precise control of&#10;biomolecular circuits, and Cybergenetics is the field&#10;dedicated to achieving this goal. A significant challenge in&#10;developing controllers for cellular functions is designing&#10;systems that can effectively manage molecular noise. To..." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#f9cb9c;strokeColor=#b45f06;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="360" y="8250" width="620" height="3570" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step7_analogy_panel" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step7" target="step7_analogy_panel"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="step_step8" value="Step 8 Inspiration Selection&#10;status: completed&#10;selected_count: 3&#10;round: 3" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="60" y="11920" width="232" height="96" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step_step7_step_step8" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step7" target="step_step8"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="step8_selected_panel" value="Step 8 Selected Inspiration&#10;count: 3&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 6&#10;domain: control_engineering&#10;radius: R2&#10;title: A computational framework for optimal and Model&#10;Predictive Control of stochastic gene regulatory networks&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['stochastic model predictive control&#10;(MPC) for gene regulatory networks', 'optimal closed-loop&#10;feedback under molecular noise', 'constraint-aware control&#10;design for biological viability', 'receding-horizon predictive&#10;coordination of biomolecular states', 'cybergenetic control&#10;architecture for cellular functions']&#10;combination_plan: Adapt the candidate’s stochastic&#10;MPC/cybergenetic framework into a unified controller for the&#10;living-material system, using noisy measurements of&#10;metabolites, genetic states, and matrix remodeling to predict&#10;future system trajectories and optimize light inputs,&#10;transport cues,...&#10;justification: The candidate provides a direct structural&#10;analogy: a predictive, optimal, noise-aware closed-loop&#10;control framework for biological regulation. This maps onto&#10;the problem’s missing unified programming layer for&#10;coordinating heterogeneous biological processes while&#10;respecting v...&#10;abstract: Engineering biology requires precise control of&#10;biomolecular circuits, and Cybergenetics is the field&#10;dedicated to achieving this goal. A significant challenge in&#10;developing controllers for cellular functions is designing&#10;systems that can effectively manage molecular noise. To...&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 3&#10;domain: computer_science&#10;radius: R2&#10;title: Towards Big Biology:: high-performance verification of&#10;large concurrent systems&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['formal verification of large concurrent&#10;systems', 'compositional model checking of interacting&#10;processes', 'temporal-logic specification of safety, liveness,&#10;and ordering constraints', 'runtime verification / closed-loop&#10;monitoring of concurrent state transitions', 'scalable&#10;abstraction-reduction methods for high-dimensional biological&#10;dynamics']&#10;combination_plan: Treat the living-material program as a&#10;concurrent system whose modules—protein-material conjugation,&#10;metabolite sensing, genetic regulation, and matrix&#10;remodeling—are verified as interacting processes with temporal&#10;constraints. Use compositional formal verification or&#10;runtime...&#10;justification: Even without the abstract, the title indicates&#10;high-performance verification of large concurrent systems,&#10;which provides a transferable abstraction for coordinating&#10;many interacting biological control loops. The problem’s core&#10;bottleneck is not just building biological parts b...&#10;abstract:&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 5&#10;domain: control_engineering&#10;radius: R2&#10;title: Systems and control theoretic approaches to engineer&#10;robust biological systems&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['closed-loop feedback control&#10;architecture for biological systems', 'robustness and&#10;stability analysis under biological uncertainty', 'predictive&#10;or model-based control for dynamic regulation', 'orthogonal&#10;control channels and modular system decomposition', 'sensing-&#10;actuation loops linking intracellular state to extracellular&#10;outputs']&#10;combination_plan: Use systems-and-control theory to formalize&#10;the living-material platform as a multi-input/multi-output&#10;closed-loop system, where molecular interfacing, metabolite&#10;sensing, genetic regulation, and matrix remodeling are modeled&#10;as coupled subsystems with feedback, feedforward, a...&#10;justification: The candidate paper’s focus on systems and&#10;control theoretic engineering of robust biological systems&#10;provides a direct transferable abstraction for the original&#10;problem’s central bottleneck: creating a unified, predictive,&#10;closed-loop programming framework across molecular, c...&#10;abstract:" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#ead1dc;strokeColor=#a64d79;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="360" y="11920" width="620" height="1608" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step8_selected_panel" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step8" target="step8_selected_panel"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="step_step9" value="Step 9 Idea Generation&#10;status: completed&#10;idea_count: 1&#10;round: 3" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="60" y="13628" width="220" height="96" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step_step8_step_step9" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step8" target="step_step9"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="step9_ideas_panel" value="Step 9 Idea Generation + Novelty Check&#10;count: 1&#10;&#10;1. Cleavage-Nucleated Condensate Controllers for Set-Point&#10;Programming of Living Hydrogel Materials&#10;novelty_level: medium&#10;motivation: Programming nonliving matter into living materials&#10;requires more than immobilizing cells; it requires a controller&#10;that senses local material state, computes a response, and&#10;resets without continuous human intervention. Hybrid sol-gel&#10;materials can host living microorganisms and connect them to&#10;inorganic/organic matrices [Author et al.,&#10;2022](https://openalex.org/W4220814513). PenTag provides site-&#10;specific covalen...&#10;methods: 1. Covalent photocleavable PenTag damage-to-signal&#10;anchor: A PenTag-compatible anchor protein is covalently&#10;attached to a living-cell hydrogel or sol-gel matrix [Author et&#10;al., 2022](https://openalex.org/W4220814513) [Author et al.,&#10;2023](https://openalex.org/W4377098401). The anchor contains, in&#10;order, a matrix-binding domain, a photocleavable peptide linker,&#10;a multivalent condensate-nucleating domain, and an effector-&#10;recognition motif. The design is inspired by photodegradable&#10;matrices that translate light int...&#10;novelty_justification: The idea is not directly anticipated by&#10;the provided references. The closest existing combination is the&#10;union of photodegradable hydrogel matrices, PenTag covalent&#10;protein-polymer conjugation, and phase-separated synthetic&#10;organelles. The photodegradable hydrogel reference supplies&#10;light-triggered matrix cleavage and spatiotemporal control of&#10;bacterial transport; PenTag supplies stable covalent anchoring&#10;of prote...&#10;improvement_suggestions: ['Sharpen the mechanistic claim by&#10;making the reset step intrinsically dependent on the repaired&#10;material state rather than on a separate protease: for example,&#10;engineer the nucleator fragment with a stiffness- or crosslink-&#10;density-sensitive degron, tension-exposed cleavage site, or&#10;mesh-size-limited sequestration mechanism so that condensate&#10;dissolution is a direct physical readout of restored matrix&#10;integrity.', 'Define a quantitative phase-diagram control law in&#10;which the critical concentration for condensate nucleation is&#10;predictably shifted by local anchor cleavage, residual anchor&#10;density, and crosslinking state. Demonstrating that condensate&#10;volume fraction is a controllable invariant across damage doses&#10;would convert the system from a component combination into a&#10;distinct embodied controller.', 'Introduce a coincidence-&#10;detection mechanism requiring two distinct cleavage products or&#10;two damage-dependent valency changes to nucleate the condensate.&#10;This would provide a sharper conceptual distinction from simple&#10;light-induced release and would make the controller selective&#10;for true damage severity rather than local concentration&#10;fluctuations.']" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="360" y="13628" width="680" height="1032" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step9_ideas_panel" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step9" target="step9_ideas_panel"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="retrieval_1" value="Retrieval 1&#10;step: step1&#10;command: search-papers&#10;cache_hit: False&#10;paper_count: 18&#10;&#10;Parameters&#10;query_text: biohybrid materials combining living cells&#10;with synthetic scaffolds&#10;keywords: [{'text': 'biohybrid materials', 'score': 10},&#10;{'text': 'materials combining', 'score': 9}, {'text':&#10;'combining living', 'score': 8}, {'text': 'living cells',&#10;'score': 7}, {'text': 'cells synthetic', 'score': 6}]&#10;source_type: idea_text&#10;top_k: 18&#10;retrieval_mode: hybrid&#10;target_field: Chemistry&#10;&#10;Returned Papers&#10;1. Synthetic Cells Revisited: Artificial Cell Construction&#10;Using Polymeric Building Blocks (2023) [score=0.7691]&#10;Abstract: The exponential growth of research on artificial&#10;cells and organelles underscores their potential as tools&#10;to advance the understanding of fundamental biological&#10;processes. The bottom-up construction from a variety of&#10;building blocks at the micro- and nanoscale, in&#10;combination...&#10;&#10;2. Preparation of Hybrid Sol-Gel Materials Based on Living&#10;Cells of Microorganisms and Their Application in&#10;Nanotechnology (2022) [score=0.5398]&#10;Abstract: Microorganism-cell-based biohybrid materials&#10;have attracted considerable attention over the last&#10;several decades. They are applied in a broad spectrum of&#10;areas, such as nanotechnologies, environmental&#10;biotechnology, biomedicine, synthetic chemistry, and&#10;bioelectronics. Sol-gel...&#10;&#10;3. Integration of a Copper-Containing Biohybrid (CuHARS)&#10;with Cellulose for Subsequent Degradation and Biomedical&#10;Control (2018) [score=0.5388]&#10;Abstract: We previously described the novel synthesis of a&#10;copper high-aspect ratio structure (CuHARS) biohybrid&#10;material using cystine. While extremely stable in water,&#10;CuHARS is completely (but slowly) degradable in cellular&#10;media. Here, integration of the CuHARS into cellulose&#10;matric...&#10;&#10;4. PenTag, a Versatile Platform for Synthesizing&#10;Protein‐Polymer Biohybrid Materials (2023) [score=0.5348]&#10;Abstract: Abstract The site‐specific and covalent&#10;conjugation of proteins on solid supports and in hydrogels&#10;is the basis for the synthesis of biohybrid materials&#10;offering broad applications. Current methods for&#10;conjugating proteins to desired targets are often&#10;challenging due to unspec...&#10;&#10;5. Multicompartment Hydrogels (2022) [score=0.5209]&#10;Abstract: Hydrogels belong to the most promising materials&#10;in polymer and materials science at the moment. As they&#10;feature soft and tissue-like character as well as high&#10;water-content, a broad range of applications are addressed&#10;with hydrogels, e.g., tissue engineering and wound&#10;dressin...&#10;&#10;6. Advancing Artificial Cells with Functional&#10;Compartmentalized Polymeric Systems - In Honor of Wolfgang&#10;Meier (2024) [score=0.5196]&#10;Abstract: The fundamental building block of living&#10;organisms is the cell, which is the universal biological&#10;base of all living entities. This micrometric mass of&#10;cytoplasm and the membrane border have fascinated&#10;scientists due to the highly complex and&#10;multicompartmentalized structure....&#10;&#10;7. Trends in the Synthesis of Polymer Nano‐ and Microscale&#10;Materials for Bio‐Related Applications (2023)&#10;[score=0.5179]&#10;Abstract: Polymeric nano- and microscale materials bear&#10;significant potential in manifold applications related to&#10;biomedicine. This is owed not only to the large chemical&#10;diversity of the constituent polymers, but also to the&#10;various morphologies these materials can achieve, ranging&#10;fro...&#10;&#10;8. Click Chemistry: A Powerful Tool to Create&#10;Polymer‐Based Macromolecular Chimeras (2008)&#10;[score=0.5175]&#10;Abstract: Abstract The combination of polymeric with&#10;biological materials, to create biohybrid macromolecules&#10;that merge the properties of both the natural and&#10;synthetic components, is a flourishing area in both life&#10;sciences and biotechnology. The click chemistry philosophy&#10;has recentl...&#10;&#10;9. Current Perspectives on Synthetic Compartments for&#10;Biomedical Applications (2022) [score=0.5124]&#10;Abstract: Nano- and micrometer-sized compartments composed&#10;of synthetic polymers are designed to mimic spatial and&#10;temporal divisions found in nature. Self-assembly of&#10;polymers into compartments such as polymersomes, giant&#10;unilamellar vesicles (GUVs), layer-by-layer (LbL)&#10;capsules, caps...&#10;&#10;10. Semiflexible polymer scaffolds: an overview of&#10;conjugation strategies (2021) [score=0.5122]&#10;Abstract: Semiflexible polymers are excellent scaffolds&#10;for the presentation of a wide variety